{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: Scope the destination finder instead of relying on `.last`**

`tapDestination` taps `find.text(label).last`, which works only because widget-tree order happens to put the `NavigationBar` label last relative to the (offstage) page content. Every placeholder page already renders the same strings as the nav labels (`Text('Home')`, `Text('Explore')`, …), so any future page that shows its label text visibly changes the match set.

Scoping the finder like the "shell offers the four destinations" test already does is explicit and order-independent:

```dart
Future<void> tapDestination(WidgetTester tester, String label) async {
  await tester.tap(
    find.descendant(of: find.byType(NavigationBar), matching: find.text(label)),
  );
  await tester.pumpAndSettle();
}
```

Also add a brief comment for why the NavigationBar scope is required.
